LiquidationPeriphery::liquidate
├── when market is not supported
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInput
└── when market is supported
    ├── when market has not authorized periphery on market
    │   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedLiquidationPeriphery
    └── given market has authorized periphery on market
        ├── it should call market.liquidate with abi.encode(periphery caller, liquidationData)
        ├── it should pass periphery caller as originalLiquidator to market for engine checks
        ├── when priority liquidation is enabled on market
        │   ├── given position is not tagged
        │   │   ├── when periphery caller is not priority liquidator
        │   │   │   └── it should revert with DlbDcfPriorityLiquidationEngineLiquidationUnauthorized
        │   │   └── when periphery caller is priority liquidator
        │   │       └── it should proceed with liquidation
        │   ├── given position is tagged by periphery caller
        │   │   ├── when within priority grace period
        │   │   │   └── it should revert with DlbDcfPriorityLiquidationEngineLiquidationUnauthorized
        │   │   └── when after priority grace period
        │   │       └── it should proceed with liquidation
        │   ├── given position is tagged by other liquidator
        │   │   ├── when within combined grace periods
        │   │   │   └── it should revert with DlbDcfPriorityLiquidationEngineLiquidationUnauthorized
        │   │   └── when after combined grace periods
        │   │       └── it should proceed with liquidation
        │   └── when current LTV is above disable priority liquidation threshold
        │       └── it should proceed with liquidation
        ├── when market is a borrow market
        │   ├── given liquidationPeripheryCallbackData is empty
        │   │   ├── it should return seized collateral, repaid borrow, and protocol fee from market
        │   │   ├── it should emit Liquidation event with periphery caller as liquidator
        │   │   ├── it should reset borrow token approval to market after liquidation
        │   │   ├── it should transfer seized collateral to the liquidator
        │   │   ├── it should liquidate via usm without calling liquidator callback
        │   │   ├── it should reset underlying approval to usm after sell
        │   │   └── it should leave periphery with zero borrow and underlying balances
        │   ├── given liquidationPeripheryCallbackData is not empty
        │   │   ├── it should return seized collateral, repaid borrow, and protocol fee from market
        │   │   ├── it should emit Liquidation event with periphery caller as liquidator
        │   │   ├── it should reset borrow token approval to market after liquidation
        │   │   ├── it should transfer seized collateral to the liquidator
        │   │   ├── it should call liquidator onLiquidationPeripheryCallback with underlying asset amount and collateral received
        │   │   ├── it should forward liquidationPeripheryCallbackData to liquidator callback
        │   │   ├── it should leave zero approval from liquidator to periphery after pull
        │   │   ├── it should reset underlying approval to usm after sell
        │   │   └── it should leave periphery with zero borrow and underlying balances
        │   ├── given stable token bought equals borrow amount to repay
        │   │   ├── it should return seized collateral, repaid borrow, and protocol fee from market
        │   │   ├── it should emit Liquidation event with periphery caller as liquidator
        │   │   ├── it should reset borrow token approval to market after liquidation
        │   │   ├── it should transfer seized collateral to the liquidator
        │   │   ├── it should not refund stable to liquidator
        │   │   ├── it should reset underlying approval to usm after sell
        │   │   └── it should leave periphery with zero borrow and underlying balances
        │   └── given stable token bought is greater than borrow amount to repay
        │       ├── it should return seized collateral, repaid borrow, and protocol fee from market
        │       ├── it should emit Liquidation event with periphery caller as liquidator
        │       ├── it should reset borrow token approval to market after liquidation
        │       ├── it should transfer seized collateral to the liquidator
        │       ├── it should refund excess stable token to liquidator
        │       ├── it should reset underlying approval to usm after sell
        │       └── it should leave periphery with zero borrow and underlying balances
        └── when market is a mint market
            ├── given liquidationPeripheryCallbackData is empty
            │   ├── it should return seized collateral, repaid borrow, and protocol fee from market
            │   ├── it should emit Liquidation event with periphery caller as liquidator
            │   ├── it should reset borrow token approval to market after liquidation
            │   ├── it should transfer seized collateral to the liquidator
            │   ├── it should liquidate via usm without calling liquidator callback
            │   ├── it should reset underlying approval to usm after sell
            │   └── it should leave periphery with zero borrow and underlying balances
            ├── given liquidationPeripheryCallbackData is not empty
            │   ├── it should return seized collateral, repaid borrow, and protocol fee from market
            │   ├── it should emit Liquidation event with periphery caller as liquidator
            │   ├── it should reset borrow token approval to market after liquidation
            │   ├── it should transfer seized collateral to the liquidator
            │   ├── it should call liquidator onLiquidationPeripheryCallback with underlying asset amount and collateral received
            │   ├── it should forward liquidationPeripheryCallbackData to liquidator callback
            │   ├── it should leave zero approval from liquidator to periphery after pull
            │   ├── it should reset underlying approval to usm after sell
            │   └── it should leave periphery with zero borrow and underlying balances
            ├── given stable token bought equals borrow amount to repay
            │   ├── it should return seized collateral, repaid borrow, and protocol fee from market
            │   ├── it should emit Liquidation event with periphery caller as liquidator
            │   ├── it should reset borrow token approval to market after liquidation
            │   ├── it should transfer seized collateral to the liquidator
            │   ├── it should not refund stable to liquidator
            │   ├── it should reset underlying approval to usm after sell
            │   └── it should leave periphery with zero borrow and underlying balances
            └── given stable token bought is greater than borrow amount to repay
                ├── it should return seized collateral, repaid borrow, and protocol fee from market
                ├── it should emit Liquidation event with periphery caller as liquidator
                ├── it should reset borrow token approval to market after liquidation
                ├── it should transfer seized collateral to the liquidator
                ├── it should refund excess stable token to liquidator
                ├── it should reset underlying approval to usm after sell
                └── it should leave periphery with zero borrow and underlying balances
